Linux packaging: make the AppImage self-contained and prove it on a distro matrix. Todo item "AppImage self-contained" in docs/ERGOPTIPLUS_TODO.md: `.zsync` and update information are done (10c016e51f, 6fb83014e3). Left: bundle the C library and loader (or build on an older base) and prove it on the distro matrix (musl cannot run glibc binaries: say so in the user-facing docs and in the refusal), keeping the tray closure. Find how the AppImage, deb/rpm and Flatpak are built (tools/build, .github/workflows/ci-linux.yml packaging jobs, linux/packaging or similar) and build them locally. If docker works in your container, run the built AppImage (extract-and-run mode, `--appimage-extract-and-run`, since FUSE is likely missing) in a matrix of distro images (ubuntu 20.04/22.04/24.04, debian 11/12, fedora latest, opensuse leap, arch, alpine to prove the musl refusal) with Xvfb, and check that it starts, shows its status window/tray, and quits cleanly. Fix what fails (one commit per cause, with a packaging test or receipt check that fails without the fix). Also: Flatpak — wmctrl is only a documented host program: check the Flatpak build and its manifest on this host if flatpak-builder can run. Never add a dependency the maintainer declined (libXi was declined).
